#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore writefile */}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/*\n"
"  DO NOT EDIT THIS CELL!!!\n"
"  This cell's content is generated automatically by a script. Anything you add\n"
"  here will be removed next time the notebook is run. To add new content, create\n"
"  a new cell before or after this one.\n"
"*/}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Package versions\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Versi pakej\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The code on this page was developed using the following requirements.\n"
"We recommend using these versions or newer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kod pada halaman ini dibangunkan menggunakan keperluan berikut.\n"
"Kami mengesyorkan penggunaan versi ini atau yang lebih baharu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Use this page to upload a workflow, run it, and get its result. The example workflow optimizes and simulates a Qiskit circuit. It simulates the circuit on classical hardware, so it does not use QPU time.\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Gunakan halaman ini untuk memuat naik workflow, menjalankannya, dan mendapatkan keputusannya. Contoh workflow ini mengoptimumkan dan mensimulasikan litar Qiskit. Ia mensimulasikan litar pada perkakasan klasik, jadi ia tidak menggunakan masa QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before you begin, [install the client package and authenticate](/guides/install-managed-workflows).\n"
msgstr "Sebelum anda bermula, [pasang pakej klien dan sahkan identiti](/guides/install-managed-workflows).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Use AI skills (optional)\">\n"
"To deploy your own code with help from an AI assistant, use the AI skills in the [Qiskit Function templates repository](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qiskit-function-templates).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Gunakan kemahiran AI (pilihan)\">\n"
"Untuk mendeploy kod anda sendiri dengan bantuan pembantu AI, gunakan kemahiran AI dalam [repositori templat Qiskit Function](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qiskit-function-templates).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write a workflow {#write-a-workflow}"
msgstr "Tulis workflow {#write-a-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create the folder structure {#create-the-folder-structure}"
msgstr "Cipta struktur folder {#create-the-folder-structure}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow is a folder of Python files with one entrypoint file. A managed workflow uploads everything in the folder, up to 50 MB, and runs the entrypoint as a script. Because a workflow uploads the whole folder, keep your local files, such as `deploy.ipynb`, outside the folder. Create the following layout:\n"
msgstr "Sebuah managed workflow ialah folder fail Python dengan satu fail titik masuk. Managed workflow memuat naik segala-galanya dalam folder, sehingga 50 MB, dan menjalankan titik masuk sebagai skrip. Oleh sebab workflow memuat naik seluruh folder, simpan fail tempatan anda, seperti `deploy.ipynb`, di luar folder tersebut. Cipta susun atur berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write the hello world entrypoint {#write-the-hello-world-entrypoint}"
msgstr "Tulis titik masuk hello world {#write-the-hello-world-entrypoint}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The entrypoint reads a circuit, optimizes and simulates it, and saves the counts and two-qubit depth. Save the following code as `source_files/hello_world.py`:\n"
msgstr "Titik masuk membaca litar, mengoptimumkan dan mensimulasikannya, serta menyimpan kiraan dan kedalaman dua-qubit. Simpan kod berikut sebagai `source_files/hello_world.py`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"If you read this page as a notebook, the code cell for `hello_world.py` starts with the `%%writefile` [magic command](https://ipython.readthedocs.io/en/stable/interactive/magics.html#cellmagic-writefile). When you run this cell, it saves the code to the file instead of running the code.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Jika anda membaca halaman ini sebagai notebook, sel kod untuk `hello_world.py` bermula dengan [arahan ajaib](https://ipython.readthedocs.io/en/stable/interactive/magics.html#cellmagic-writefile) `%%writefile`. Apabila anda menjalankan sel ini, ia menyimpan kod ke dalam fail dan bukannya menjalankan kod tersebut.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The entrypoint uses three functions from `qiskit_serverless`:\n"
msgstr "Titik masuk menggunakan tiga fungsi daripada `qiskit_serverless`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`get_arguments()` returns the keyword arguments that you pass to `run()`, as a dictionary. Each value must be JSON-serializable, or an object that the client can encode, such as a `QuantumCircuit`. Encoded objects arrive as the same objects that you passed.\n"
msgstr "`get_arguments()` mengembalikan argumen kata kunci yang anda hantar kepada `run()`, sebagai kamus. Setiap nilai mestilah boleh diserialisasi JSON, atau objek yang boleh dikodkan oleh klien, seperti `QuantumCircuit`. Objek yang dikodkan tiba sebagai objek yang sama seperti yang anda hantar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`update_status(Job.OPTIMIZING_HARDWARE)` sets the detailed status `RUNNING: OPTIMIZING_FOR_HARDWARE`, which you can see while the job runs. See [Report progress with update_status()](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status).\n"
msgstr "`update_status(Job.OPTIMIZING_HARDWARE)` menetapkan status terperinci `RUNNING: OPTIMIZING_FOR_HARDWARE`, yang boleh anda lihat semasa job berjalan. Lihat [Laporkan kemajuan dengan update_status()](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`save_result()` stores a JSON-serializable value that you read later with `job.result()`. The workflow returns the counts as a dictionary and the two-qubit depth of the optimized circuit as an integer.\n"
msgstr "`save_result()` menyimpan nilai yang boleh diserialisasi JSON yang anda baca kemudian dengan `job.result()`. Workflow mengembalikan kiraan sebagai kamus dan kedalaman dua-qubit bagi litar yang dioptimumkan sebagai integer.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anything that the workflow writes to standard output, such as the two-qubit depth, goes to the job's logs. To add timestamps and log levels, use the `logging` module. See [Write logs and handle errors](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors).\n"
msgstr "Apa-apa sahaja yang ditulis oleh workflow ke output standard, seperti kedalaman dua-qubit, akan masuk ke log job. Untuk menambah cap masa dan tahap log, gunakan modul `logging`. Lihat [Tulis log dan kendalikan ralat](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload the workflow {#upload-the-workflow}"
msgstr "Muat naik workflow {#upload-the-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In your local notebook, run the following code from the `hello_world_project` folder. The code connects with your saved account, defines the workflow, and uploads it. `entrypoint` is the file that the workflow runs, and `working_dir` is the folder that you upload:\n"
msgstr "Dalam notebook tempatan anda, jalankan kod berikut daripada folder `hello_world_project`. Kod ini bersambung dengan akaun tersimpan anda, mentakrifkan workflow, dan memuat naiknya. `entrypoint` ialah fail yang dijalankan oleh workflow, dan `working_dir` ialah folder yang anda muat naik:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the workflow with inputs {#run-the-workflow-with-inputs}"
msgstr "Jalankan workflow dengan input {#run-the-workflow-with-inputs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Construct a three-qubit GHZ circuit to pass to `hello_world` as an input:\n"
msgstr "Bina litar GHZ tiga-qubit untuk dihantar kepada `hello_world` sebagai input:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run `hello_world` with the circuit and the number of shots as keyword arguments. The argument names match the keys that the entrypoint reads with `get_arguments()`:\n"
msgstr "Jalankan `hello_world` dengan litar dan bilangan shot sebagai argumen kata kunci. Nama argumen sepadan dengan kunci yang dibaca oleh titik masuk dengan `get_arguments()`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`run()` returns a `Job` after the workflow queues the job. It does not wait for the job to run. The job continues in the cloud after you close your Python session. To find it again later, list your recent jobs with `client.jobs()`.\n"
msgstr "`run()` mengembalikan `Job` selepas workflow meletakkan job dalam baris gilir. Ia tidak menunggu job berjalan. Job diteruskan dalam awan selepas anda menutup sesi Python anda. Untuk mencarinya semula kemudian, senaraikan job terkini anda dengan `client.jobs()`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: add the web UI for job history when it is available. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get the status, result, and logs {#get-the-status-result-and-logs}"
msgstr "Dapatkan status, keputusan, dan log {#get-the-status-result-and-logs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Immediately after you call `run()`, the status is usually `QUEUED`:\n"
msgstr "Sejurus selepas anda memanggil `run()`, status biasanya `QUEUED`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The status changes from `QUEUED` to `INITIALIZING`, `RUNNING`, and then `DONE`.\n"
msgstr "Status berubah daripada `QUEUED` kepada `INITIALIZING`, `RUNNING`, dan kemudian `DONE`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.result()` waits until the job ends, then returns the value that the workflow passed to `save_result()`:\n"
msgstr "`job.result()` menunggu sehingga job tamat, kemudian mengembalikan nilai yang dihantar oleh workflow kepada `save_result()`:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/managed-workflows/deploy-first-managed-workflow/extracted-outputs/b4e7a2fe-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/managed-workflows/deploy-first-managed-workflow/extracted-outputs/b4e7a2fe-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can read the logs while the job runs. The workflow uploads new lines about every 15 seconds. The logs include the line that the workflow printed:\n"
msgstr "Anda boleh membaca log semasa job berjalan. Workflow memuat naik baris baharu kira-kira setiap 15 saat. Log merangkumi baris yang dicetak oleh workflow:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Update the workflow {#update-the-workflow}"
msgstr "Kemas kini workflow {#update-the-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To change a workflow, edit its files and call `upload()` again with the same `title`. The new upload replaces the earlier one, and jobs that already started are not affected.\n"
msgstr "Untuk menukar workflow, edit failnya dan panggil `upload()` sekali lagi dengan `title` yang sama. Muat naik baharu menggantikan yang terdahulu, dan job yang telah bermula tidak terjejas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fields such as `arguments_schema` and `sizes_map` keep their stored values when you omit them from the new upload.\n"
msgstr "Medan seperti `arguments_schema` dan `sizes_map` mengekalkan nilai tersimpannya apabila anda mengabaikannya daripada muat naik baharu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Langkah seterusnya {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- [Define inputs and outputs](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs) to learn which argument and result types a workflow supports.\n"
"- [Declare dependencies](/guides/managed-workflow-dependencies) to use more Python packages in your workflow.\n"
"- [Run quantum jobs from a workflow](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows) to run your circuits on a QPU, report each stage, and track the QPU jobs.\n"
"- [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow) to learn all job statuses, debug a failed job, and find a job later.\n"
"- To start from working code, deploy one of the [Qiskit Function templates](/guides/qiskit-function-templates), or adapt a template for your own workflow.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Cadangan\">\n"
"- [Takrifkan input dan output](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs) untuk mengetahui jenis argumen dan keputusan yang disokong oleh workflow.\n"
"- [Isytiharkan kebergantungan](/guides/managed-workflow-dependencies) untuk menggunakan lebih banyak pakej Python dalam workflow anda.\n"
"- [Jalankan job kuantum daripada workflow](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows) untuk menjalankan litar anda pada QPU, melaporkan setiap peringkat, dan menjejak job QPU.\n"
"- [Jalankan managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow) untuk mempelajari semua status job, menyahpepijat job yang gagal, dan mencari job kemudian.\n"
"- Untuk bermula daripada kod yang berfungsi, deploy salah satu [templat Qiskit Function](/guides/qiskit-function-templates), atau sesuaikan templat untuk workflow anda sendiri.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
